WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.680
Long ago, humans realized that living things
are made of cells.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.060
Moving, replicating, blobs of water, which,
when arranged just right, produce a bigger

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.080
blob that moves, and replicates, and makes
YouTube videos.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.120
And then a biologist boarded a boat called
the Beagle to better understand the beaks

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.120
of birds.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.500
He noticed that islands rich with seeds were
home to short-beaked birds,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.420
And where fish were far and wide, so too were
beaks.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.789
And since birds don’t change beaks like
humans and hats, he had discovered natural

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:27.789
selection.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:32.419
But this study of how incredible living organisms
emerge from very simple, microscopic things

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:34.609
is really a story of economics.

00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:39.989
Wherever resources are limited, the same basic
laws apply - whether in ants, plants, or Fortune

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:41.370
500 companies.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.690
Living organisms are running economic simulations
that can help answer some of our biggest questions.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.040
This is the Biology of Business.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.000
The goal of a business, like any organism, is to stay alive

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.660
Yet they’ll set up camp even in the darkest,
dirtiest places.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:00.809
So why live in the extreme cold?

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:04.680
And why buy and sell human organs when there’s
easier money to be made?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.540
Because economic laws make these places desirable.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.979
If there are too many penguins, they starve
and recover until a sustainable number is

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:12.979
reached.

00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:15.180
In extreme environments, that number is very
low.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.500
So it might suck to live in the Antarctic,
but there’s so little competition that it’s

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.500
worth adapting.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.770
And as long as there’s demand for corrupt
and distasteful services, so too will businesses

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.409
be willing to provide them.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:31.600
That’s because prices naturally rise until
someone will make a deal, and someone always

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.600
will.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.270
And in every environment, organisms have different
strategies for survival.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.859
Rats and mice are really just genetic batons,
passing on their genes as quickly as possible

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:42.119
to many children.

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:46.280
No need for private rat school, they play
the numbers game, betting that at least one

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.670
will be successful.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.420
Elephants prefer to invest in just a few children,
which they gestate for nearly two years.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.020
And companies are no different.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.659
Many see Amazon as disorganized, this week
announcing a phone designed for… no-one?

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:00.909
and next a button for buying pop tarts.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:05.119
And others think Apple is too slow at entering
markets and adding features - putting their

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:07.030
eggs in so few baskets.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.890
But these aren’t failures of management,
just different strategies for survival.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.000
Amazon takes the mouse approach of trying
a bunch of products in hopes that some will

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.000
succeed.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.920
Apple is the elephant, investing very heavily
in only a few products, which are late to

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:20.970
enter the market.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:25.390
But surely not all strategies are equally
efficient, so which organism will win the

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.880
game of evolution?

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.920
And what does the perfect business look like?

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.110
Well, there’s no finale to evolution because
as the environment changes, so too does natural

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.110
selection.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:39.530
And the features that make a good species
in one environment are detrimental in another.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.410
There will probably never be a single, all-powerful
Buy-N-Large corporation because different

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.600
markets require different adaptations.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.840
It’s easy to think
of evolution as a force that needs no controlling,

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:56.150
that better businesses and species will thrive
naturally.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.310
But evolution is blind to all but one fact:
does this gene increase or decrease the chance

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.210
that its host will reproduce?

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.830
It doesn’t know if it also hurts the group
as a whole.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:11.120
Irish Elk are a good example: Bigger antlers
attracted more mates, which began an evolutionary

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.690
arms race of all antlers getting bigger.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:18.320
But what evolution didn’t know was how much
of a burden these huge antlers would become.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.640
Every elk would be better off if all their
antlers were half as big, but no individual

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.360
elk could do so and still find a mate.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.000
Likewise, market forces can shape businesses
in a way that hurts everyone but no individual

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.180
business could resist and stay competitive.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.300
All of this means that you are guided by markets
like ants are guided by evolution.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:42.600
But it also means we have millions of accidental
economic experiments in nature, just waiting

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.480
to be explored.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.750
